---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="Ravikumar Buragapu is an engineering leader focused on AI engineering, agentic systems, platform engineering, and building reliable, secure, production-ready enterprise platforms."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>About</h1>

			{/* Headshot: add a photo to the project's public folder (for example
			    public/ravikumar.jpg), then remove the comment markers around this line.
			<img class="headshot" src="/ravikumar.jpg" alt="Ravikumar Buragapu" width="160" height="160" />
			*/}

			<p>
				I'm a Director of Engineering focused on AI engineering, platform
				engineering, and reliability at enterprise scale. My work centers on
				turning emerging technologies—from GenAI to agentic systems—into
				production-ready platforms that are secure, observable, resilient,
				and built to operate at scale.
			</p>

			<p>
				I believe the next phase of AI will be defined not just by what models
				can do, but by how well we engineer the systems around them:
				identity, evaluation, permissions, infrastructure, operational
				controls, and human accountability.
			</p>

			<h2 id="work">What I work on</h2>
			<p>
				My focus spans AI infrastructure, agentic architectures, LLM
				inference, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), cloud platforms,
				site reliability engineering (SRE), and operational intelligence.
				I work at the intersection of architecture, engineering execution,
				and operations—with an emphasis on making complex systems reliable,
				secure, and measurable in production.
			</p>

			<h2 id="arc">Engineering leadership and impact</h2>
			<ul class="arc">
				<li>
					<strong>Oracle Health</strong>
					<p>
						I lead engineering across infrastructure, reliability, and
						data intelligence platforms spanning commercial, regulated,
						and Federal environments, modernizing them into AI-native,
						action-driven platforms with the operational foundations
						required for secure, highly available, data-intensive
						services.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Wells Fargo</strong>
					<p>
						I formed the Agentic and GenAI Squad, headed the AI-native
						SDLC transformation, and helped define the architecture and
						strategy for agentic workflows across engineering, reaching
						more than 10,000 developers.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Adobe</strong>
					<p>
						I led platform engineering and the Agentic AI Builders Group,
						and built an AI-driven Service Maturity Insights platform. My
						work there included an AI-native developer platform with a
						modern, action-driven CI/CD approach.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Kohl's</strong>
					<p>
						I worked on AI initiatives and the development of a data
						science engineering platform.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Earlier</strong>
					<p>
						Engineering roles at Charles Schwab, after beginning my
						software engineering career in India in 2000.
					</p>
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 id="perspective">Technical perspective</h2>
			<p>
				I’m particularly interested in the engineering principles that
				make AI systems trustworthy and operationally sustainable:
				explicit agent identity, least-privilege access, policy-as-code,
				reproducible evaluation, observability, controlled autonomy,
				and reliable failure recovery.
			</p>

			<p>
				I also care about the broader engineering system—developer
				experience, platform abstractions, automation, and operational
				practices that help teams deliver software faster without
				compromising reliability or security.
			</p>

			<h2 id="convictions">How I think</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Autonomy should be earned.</strong> An agent's freedom to
					act should rise and fall with measured evidence of reliability,
					not with enthusiasm.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Evaluation is the control plane.</strong> The same system
					that measures an agent should decide what it is allowed to do.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Agents are a reliability problem.</strong> Identity,
					observability, error budgets, and rollback are old platform
					disciplines applied to systems that can now take action.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 id="education">Education and credentials</h2>

			<section class="education-credentials">
				<h3>Education</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>
						Incoming Ph.D. Student in Artificial Intelligence
					</li>
					<li>
						Executive MBA — Quantic School of Business and Technology
					</li>
					<li>
						M.Sc. in Physics (Electronics specialization) — Andhra University
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>Professional certifications</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>Google Cloud Professional Cloud Architect</li>
					<li>AWS Certified Solutions Architect – Professional</li>
					<li>Certified Cloud Security Professional (CCSP)</li>
					<li>ITIL Master</li>
					<li>IAPP Artificial Intelligence Governance Professional (AIGP)</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<h2 id="more">Speaking, writing, and projects</h2>
			<p>
				I have spoken at DPE Summit, Percona Community Live, and
				ScyllaDB Summit, as well as AI and machine learning panels
				in Santa Clara. My writing explores developer productivity,
				platform engineering, AI governance, and the architectural
				and operational challenges of running AI agents in production.
				My open-source projects focus on measuring and controlling AI
				systems in practice.
			</p>

			<p>
				<a href="/speak">Speaking</a>
				·
				<a href="/writing">Writing</a>
				·
				<a href="/projects">Projects</a>
			</p>

			<p>
				To get in touch, message me on
				<a
					href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ravikumar-buragapu"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
				>LinkedIn</a>.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.arc {
		list-style: none;
		padding: 0;
		margin: 1rem 0;
	}
	.arc li {
		padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
		border-left: 3px solid rgb(var(--gray-light));
	}
	.arc p {
		margin: 0.25rem 0 0 0;
	}
	.headshot {
		float: right;
		margin: 0 0 1rem 1.5rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		object-fit: cover;
	}
</style>